        <section id="what-is-wegovy">
          <h2>What is Wegovy?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy® is popular brand of weight loss medicine. It contains Semaglutide, which is an active ingredient in Wegovy. This is used to treat Type 2 diabetes but also helps in weight loss treatment in  patients suffering from obesity with a BMI higher than 30 or a BMI of 27 and over for anyone with weight related health conditions such as hypertension or type 2 diabetes. It is most effective when used alongside a balanced diet and physical exercise over a long period of time.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="who-is-eligible-for-wegovy">
          <h2>Who is eligible for Wegovy UK?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy prescription medication is usually recommended for individuals:</p>
              <ul>
              <li>Over 18 years old that are obese. (BMI over 30)</li>
              <li>With a BMI higher than 27 due to health conditions such as high blood pressure, diabetes, etc.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="how-to-get-wegovy-prescription">
          <h2>How to get a Wegovy Prescription?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>If you are looking to buy Wegovy online in the UK, you would require valid prescription provided by health care professionals. You can start taking an online consultation and answering the clinical questionnaire which will be evaluated by our prescribers to make sure you qualify for this weight loss treatment.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="how-does-wegovy-work">
          <h2>How does Wegovy work?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy (Semaglutide) acts a natural hormone - glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP 1) targets certain areas in the brain which control the appetite and blood sugar levels in your body. It gives you a feeling of fullness and reduces food cravings resulting in reduced intake of food leading to weight loss. It is a prefilled injectable pen with 4 doses, with one dose once weekly for 4 weeks, lasting for one month of treatment.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="how-long-does-wegovy-take-to-work">
          <h2>How long does Wegovy take to work?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>If you are taking Wegovy for first time, you often experience changes in appetite and noticeable weight loss within the first few weeks. Studies show that an average body weight reduction of  5% within a month. Usually, the weight loss with Wegovy is steady and some may achieve significant weight loss depending on age, dosage, etc</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="wegovy-dosage-chart">
          <h2>Wegovy Dosage Chart</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Following the regular wegovy dosage plan is necessary to ensure medication is taken consistently to achieve effective weight loss and minimising the side effects. Starting with a lower dose of 0.25 mg for the first 4 weeks helps your body adjust with the medication. After this initial period, the dose can be increased to 0.5 mg per week or higher, depending on your response to the treatment. It would take 4 to 5 weeks to reach a "steady state," where the drug concentration in your body remains consistent. It is advisable to consult your healthcare provider before increasing the doses.</p>
 
          <p><img src="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/media/wysiwyg/wegovy-dose-schedule.png" data-original="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/media/wysiwyg/wegovy-dose-schedule.png" id="NEIUDPF" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" alt="" class="mf-loaded" data-was-processed="true">
             
           </p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="how-to-inject-wegovy">
          <h2>How to Inject Wegovy?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy (semaglutide) should be injected under the skin once a week on the same day, at any time of the day, before or after food intake. The recommended wegovy dose for first time users is 0.25mg per week and must slowly increase over 20 weeks to maintain dose of 2.4 mg. This would help in minimizing the side effects. Each pen contains four doses lasting for a month.</p>
<p><strong>Administering the injection:</strong> Hold the Wegovy pen at a 90-degree angle against the skin, ensuring it is firmly pressed against the injection site. Press the button to deliver the medication. The injection process may take a few seconds. Once complete, remove the pen from the skin.</p>
<p>By choosing fleshy areas of body such as upper arms, thighs or stomach (abdomen) can help the injection to hurt less. It is advised not to inject into your muscle or vein. It is better to shift injection sites to minimize discomfort and ensure optimal absorption.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section id="best-place-inject-wegovy">
          <h2>Best place to inject Wegovy</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <ul>
<li>Upper arms: The fleshy area on the front of your upper arm above the elbow - however, this may not be the most comfortable way to administer your injection.</li>
<li>Upper thighs: Similar to the upper arm, the front of your thigh provides ample injection space and often feels less sensitive. Injecting in the upper thigh can be more comfortable and easier to reach than the upper arm.</li>
<li>Stomach (abdomen): The lower abdomen, two inches away from your belly button, can be another suitable location. However, consult your doctor for guidance if you have concerns about skin sensitivity in this area.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you're still struggling to figure out where you should inject, it is better to divide the injection site into four separate sections. For each dosage you can pick one of the sections and rotate between them until all four injections have been used. Also, if you are injecting in a similar spot on the upper arm or thigh, you can insert the wegovy pen at least one finger width away from your previous injection site.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="wegovy-side-effects">
          <h2>Wegovy side effects</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
          <p>Like any medications using Wegovy causes side effects that often happens within the gastro-intestinal tract. These include nausea, Diarrhoea, Vomiting, Constipation etc. Other mild side effects can be headaches, abdominal pain, tiredness, heartburn, sore throat etc. All these side effects should disappear within few weeks on its own. If it becomes severe, then consulting your doctor or pharmacist is important.</p>
<p>Serious side effects such as Low blood sugar levels (type 2 diabetes), Pancreatitis, Gall bladder problems, Diabetic eye problems, Risk of thyroid cancer, etc are reported in some cases.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="looking-wegovy-alternatives">
          <h2>Looking for Wegovy alternatives?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Some patients have medical conditions which may not be suitable for using wegovy. Other factors may include cost, availability or side effects. Also, few may prefer oral medications over injections for weight loss treatments. You can explore the other treatment options provided below which would help you finding the right medication.</p>
<p><a tabindex="0" href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/mounjaro.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Mounjaro</strong> </a>- Both Wegovy and Mounjaro are used for weight loss treatment in the UK. Mounjaro (Trizepatide) utilises dual action performance, as GLP 1 and GIP agonist are approved for type 2 diabetes management and weight loss alike.</p>
<p><a tabindex="0" href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/ozempic.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Ozempic</strong> </a>– The active ingredient in Wegovy, Semaglutide, is also found in Ozempic which controls the appetite and makes you feel satiety. The main difference is Wegovy has been officially licensed for weight loss while Ozempic is approved only for type 2 diabetes patients to manage their blood glucose levels.</p>
<p><a tabindex="0" href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/saxenda.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Saxenda</strong> </a>– Wegovy and Saxenda are injectable pens have similar functions and side effects. But the key difference are active ingredient, frequency of dosages, etc</p>
<p><a tabindex="0" href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/orlistat-xenical-capsules.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Orlistat</strong> </a>- It is available in form of capsules which absorbs up to 33% less fat from your diet aiding in weight loss for obese patients.</p>
          </div>
        </section>


        <section id="wegovy-cardiovascular-health">
          <h2>Wegovy and Cardiovascular Health</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>It is common that with obesity, the body faces a number of knock-on effects from this one condition. One of these, and arguably the most detrimental, is cardiovascular health. Patients who are overweight or obese have an increased risk of heart-related issues, like heart attacks, strokes and are at risk of dying early. </p>
            <h3>1. How does Wegovy help improve cardiovascular health?</h3>
            <p>Wegovy encourages weight loss, which lowers blood sugar, LDL cholesterol, and high blood pressure—all major cardiovascular risk factors. Semaglutide also directly lowers inflammation and enhances endothelial function, both of which promote heart health. Wegovy can help you lose weight and improve your cardiovascular health over time when combined with lifestyle modifications like diet and exercise.</p>
            <h3>2. Has Wegovy been studied for its effects on cardiovascular events?</h3>
            <p>Indeed, Wegovy's effects on cardiovascular events and weight loss efficacy have been examined in the STEP and SELECT studies. In people who are overweight or obese, the <a href="https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(24)01498-3/fulltext" target="_blank">SELECT</a> study showed a significant decrease in major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE), including heart attacks, strokes, and cardiovascular deaths.</p>
              <h3>3. How quickly can cardiovascular benefits from Wegovy be observed?</h3>
              <p>After beginning Wegovy, weight, blood pressure, and cholesterol levels can all improve in a matter of weeks to months. Multi-year trials like SELECT have demonstrated that reductions in cardiovascular risks, such as heart attacks or strokes, may become apparent over longer time periods. Nevertheless, since each person is unique, outcomes from certain trials and control groups may not always be replicated. You should see favorable outcomes if you keep your drug regimen regular and concentrate on your food and exercise.</p>
              <h3>4. Can Wegovy lower blood pressure?</h3>
              <p>Systolic and diastolic blood pressure are substantially decreased by Wegovy. In order to further improve cardiovascular and weight-related benefits, weight loss is primarily achieved by lowering the burden on the heart and improving vascular resistance by regular medication administration and suitable lifestyle modifications. By acting on GLP-1 receptors, semaglutide also promotes vasodilation, which lowers blood pressure. Clinical research has demonstrated that even slight weight loss with Wegovy is linked to quantifiable improvements in hypertension. Wegovy is an appealing option for people with high blood pressure and obesity because of these two benefits. Lower blood pressure improves cardiovascular health overall by lowering the risk of cardiovascular events including heart attacks and strokes.</p>
              <h3>5. Does Wegovy improve cholesterol levels?</h3>
              <p>Wegovy has a favorable effect on cholesterol levels, helping lower LDL cholesterol and triglycerides while slightly raising HDL cholesterol. These changes are crucial for reducing the risk of atherosclerosis, a condition where plaque buildup narrows arteries and increases the risk of cardiovascular events. Weight loss achieved with Wegovy reduces lipid accumulation in the liver and improves lipid metabolism.</p>

              <h3>6. Can Wegovy reduce the risk of heart attack or stroke?</h3>
              <p>Wegovy has a positive impact on cholesterol levels, assisting in the reduction of triglycerides and LDL cholesterol while somewhat increasing HDL cholesterol. Atherosclerosis, a disorder where plaque accumulation narrows arteries and raises the risk of cardiovascular events, can be prevented with these modifications. Wegovy-induced weight loss enhances lipid metabolism and decreases hepatic lipid buildup.</p>
          </div>
        </section>


